# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

Each Legacy card (`traininggrounds-041`–`060`) draws its own picture on both faces: the set's yard under its Core card's subject, kept where the Core picture puts it, plus a practice-yard touch no other Legacy card has. Radiant only gilds and adds rays; a fixture proves every Core and other Training Grounds picture unchanged; with ruling R2724000, a `--visual` fragment and a pixel spec. The planner prototyped all of it on this base: tests, typecheck, eslint and `typecheck:component` passed, and the pixel spec failed on today's code, as it must.

## Files to touch

| Path | | What |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/cards/art/fixtures/art-before-2724.json` | new | recorded in step 1, before any code change |
| `apps/web/src/cards/art/procedural.ts` | change | `ArtSpec.subjectRidges`, `FIGURE_GROUND_LAYERS` |
| `apps/web/src/cards/art/traininggrounds.ts` | change | `export type Paint`, `backdrop(night)`, `VIGNETTE`, `SVG_OPEN`, Legacy section, comments |
| `apps/web/src/cards/art/svg.ts` | change | `legacyArtUri` |
| `apps/web/src/cards/art/CardArt.tsx` | change | Legacy branch, own-id real art, family `legacy` |
| `apps/web/src/cards/art/traininggrounds.test.tsx` | change | R2724000 tests |
| `apps/web/src/cards/art/ART.md` | change | Training Grounds paragraph |
| `e2e/cypress/component/legacy-art.cy.tsx` | new | pixel spec |
| `spec/rulings/R2724000.md` | new | the ruling |
| `spec/rulings/R2202000.md`, `spec/rulings/R2511000.md` | change | one sentence each |
| `spec/pending/2724.md` | new | §11 paragraph |
| `crates/cards/patches/pending/<slug>.json` | new | from `cargo jackioh patches` |

Nothing else: not `spec/11-rulings.md`, `spec/INDEX.md` (no `spec index`), crate code, the catalog, the other art files or fixtures, `.github/`, `.harness/`, `bot/`. Governing: R503, R2202000, R2511000, R2529000; CLAUDE.md rules 3, 7, 9.

## Steps

1. **Record the fixture on the untouched code.** `sh scripts/build-wasm.sh`, then create the temporary `apps/web/src/cards/art/record-2724.test.ts`:
   ```ts
   import{writeFileSync}from"node:fs";import{dirname,join}from"node:path";import{fileURLToPath}from"node:url";import{it}from"vitest";
   import{CATALOG}from"@jackioh/cards";import type{CardDef}from"@jackioh/shared";
   import{hashId}from"./hash.ts";import{motifFor}from"./motifs.ts";import{proceduralArtUri,trainingGroundsArtUri}from"./svg.ts";import{compositionFor,themeFor}from"./themes.ts";import{isTrainingGroundsArt,snapshotArtOf}from"./traininggrounds.ts";
   function pictureOf(card:CardDef,radiant:boolean):string{if(isTrainingGroundsArt(card.id))return trainingGroundsArtUri(card.id,card.name,card.tags,card.type,radiant);const theme=themeFor(card.tags,card.type);return proceduralArtUri(card.id,theme,compositionFor(card.type),radiant,motifFor(card.name,theme));}
   it("records",()=>{const kept=Object.values(CATALOG).filter((c)=>(c.set==="Core"||c.set==="Training Grounds")&&snapshotArtOf(c.id)===null).sort((a,b)=>(a.id<b.id?-1:1));
   const lines=kept.map((c)=>`  "${c.id}": [${hashId(pictureOf(c,false))}, ${hashId(pictureOf(c,true))}]`);
   writeFileSync(join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)),"fixtures/art-before-2724.json"),`{\n${lines.join(",\n")}\n}\n`);});
   ```
   Run `pnpm --dir apps/web exec vitest run src/cards/art/record-2724.test.ts` and delete the file. Expect 152 entries, first `"core-001": [1291945059, 4082561380]`, last `"traininggrounds-040": [3846876193, 4244789349]`; anything else means the code was already changed.

2. **`procedural.ts`.** In `type ArtSpec` after `motifGlyphs`, add `subjectRidges: readonly [number, number];` with a doc comment: R2724000, where the composition's subject lies in `ridges` as `[from, to)` (a figure without its two hills, a burst's or sigil's every layer, none of a landscape's); `artSvg` ignores it. Above `const FIGURE_STANCE` add `/** R2724000: a figure's first two layers are its hills, ground and not subject. */ const FIGURE_GROUND_LAYERS = 2;`. In `artSpec`, after `const geometry: Geometry = {…};`:
   ```ts
   // R2724000: the composition's own layers follow the backdrop, the twist under it and the circuits.
   const subjectFrom = behind.length + twist.under.length + circuitsUnder.length;
   const subjectTo = subjectFrom + composed.layers.length;
   const ground = composition === "figure" ? FIGURE_GROUND_LAYERS : composition === "landscape" ? composed.layers.length : 0;
   ```
   and after `motifGlyphs,` in the returned object: `subjectRidges: [Math.min(subjectFrom + ground, subjectTo), subjectTo],`.

3. **`traininggrounds.ts`, same-output refactors.** Add `import { artSpec, type ArtSpec, type SkyScheme } from "./procedural.ts";` and `compositionFor`, `themeFor` to the `./themes.ts` import. `type Paint` → `export type Paint`. `backdrop`'s third parameter becomes `night: boolean` (delete its `const night = …` line). Under `// The document` add `const VIGNETTE =` and `const SVG_OPEN =`, holding verbatim the `<radialGradient id="v" …>` string `trainingGroundsSvg` pushes and its `<svg viewBox=…>` opening; there use `defs.push(VIGNETTE)`, `SVG_OPEN +` and `backdrop(behind, p, FAMILY_PAINTS[subject.family].sky === NIGHT_SKY, defs)`. Reword the header, `SNAPSHOT_ART` and `snapshotArtOf` comments: Legacy cards draw their Core card's subject in the yard with a touch of their own (R2724000, `legacySvg`).

4. **`traininggrounds.ts`, Legacy section**, appended under `// R2724000: the Legacy cards' own pictures`, each constant with a one-line doc comment (space the code in the file's style):
   ```ts
   export const LEGACY_PAINT:Paint={sky:DAY_SKY,ground:SAND,wood:WOOD,light:"#f2e6c8",body:"#e0c060",dark:"#5a3a1a",accent:"#d2452f",glow:"#fff2c0",line:OUTLINE};
   const LEGACY_SKIES:Readonly<Record<SkyScheme,readonly [string,string]>>={dawn:DAY_SKY,split:DAY_SKY,dusk:DUSK_SKY,night:NIGHT_SKY};
   const LEGACY_WOOD_MIX=0.4; const LEGACY_INK=0.5; const LEGACY_GLOW_SHARE=0.5; const PATCH_RADIUS=0.62; const PATCH_STITCH=0.82; const PATCH_STITCH_DASH="1.4 1.1";
   const GLYPH_STROKE=1.1; const ACCENT_OPACITY=0.8; const TOUCH_INSET=17; const TOUCH_GROUND=86;
   const CARROT="#e8742a"; const LEAF="#5ab84a"; const CHALKBOARD="#2f4a3a"; const STONE="#9a9488"; const WATER="#4a9ad8"; const FIG="#6a2a5a";
   export type LegacyTouch="rope-cordon"|"crate-stack"|"sword-in-sand"|"paw-prints"|"weapon-rack"|"arrow-target"|"range-flags"|"straw-heap"|"hammock"|"lantern"|"scratching-post"|"carrot-bucket"|"chalk-tally"|"lifting-stone"|"tattered-banner"|"shovel"|"water-barrel"|"pell-post"|"fig-basket"|"scarecrow";
   ```
   `export const LEGACY_TOUCHES: Readonly<Record<string, LegacyTouch>>`: one line per id, `traininggrounds-041` to `-060` in order, the n-th id taking the union's n-th member (041 rope-cordon … 060 scarecrow). Then exactly:
   ```ts
   function pawPrint(p:Paint,x:number,y:number):string{const ink={opacity:0.75};return ellipse(x,y,1.6,1.3,p.dark,ink)+circle(x-1.6,y-1.8,0.6,p.dark,ink)+circle(x,y-2.4,0.6,p.dark,ink)+circle(x+1.6,y-1.8,0.6,p.dark,ink);}
   export const TOUCH_DRAWINGS: Readonly<Record<LegacyTouch,(p:Paint)=>string>> = {
   "rope-cordon":(p)=>rect(-12,-12,3,12,p.wood,inked(p))+rect(9,-12,3,12,p.wood,inked(p))+path("M-10.5 -10Q0 -3 10.5 -10","none",{stroke:p.dark,"stroke-width":1.4,"stroke-linecap":"round"}),
   "crate-stack":(p)=>rect(-12,-9,11,9,p.wood,inked(p))+rect(1,-9,11,9,p.wood,inked(p))+rect(-5.5,-18,11,9,p.wood,inked(p))+path("M-12 -9L-1 0M1 -9L12 0M-5.5 -18L5.5 -9","none",{stroke:p.dark,"stroke-width":0.7}),
